# Performance

- Default to Server Components; split Client Components at interaction boundaries.
- Lazy-load heavy client modules and below-the-fold UI when bundle analysis or UX warrants it.
- Use Next.js image and font optimization; avoid loading entire icon packs for one icon.
- Minimize unnecessary re-renders: stable keys, memo only with measured need.
- Cache and revalidate data fetching deliberately (`fetch` options, Next cache tags when applicable).
- Every optimization should have a stated reason (bundle size, LCP, interaction latency)—not speculative micro-tuning.
